# Generated by `artemis build --lang=python` from testdata/corpus/empty.art.
#
# This is a ONE-WAY EXPORT. Artemis does not read it back: the .art file is the
# source of truth, and running the command again overwrites this file. Once you
# decide to own this instead, edit it freely and stop generating it.
#
# Where this differs from `artemis run` on the same scenario:
#   - a comparison uses Python's rules, so `status == "200"` does not hold
#     against a JSON 200 the way it does under the interpreter;
#   - a step that wrote no `timeout` has none here; artemis applies a default of
#     its own per step type;
#   - stdout and stderr are not truncated; artemis caps them for its report;
#   - a variable with no value raises at the point of use. `artemis run`
#     reports all of them before the first step; an exported module has no
#     such moment.
